all right good evening i'm lieutenant  ray spencer i'm the homicide lieutenant  with the las vegas metropolitan police  department i'm out here this evening to  brief you on a homicide investigation  that we are conducting in the 5000 block  of sage lynn  street which is a residential  neighborhood near the intersections of  boulder highway and tropicana i stress  the details that i'm sharing right now  are very preliminary but around 5 pm  tonight metro police responded on report  of a male who had been shot  inside the residence directly behind me  patrol officers arrived and they  observed a male who was deceased inside  the doorway the original details that we  were provided is that the suspect who  was believed to be  the son of the deceased  would was potentially inside the  residence that prompted officers to try  to get him to exit  and at that point notification was made  to our swat team who responded metro  swat officers cleared the residence and  discovered that there was no one else  inside the house other than the deceased  male the deceased male is a black male  in his mid 60s and at this point we  believe our suspect is going to be his  son who is a black male in his early  thirties  what we've learned up to this point is  that the suspect lives in the house  behind me by himself  apparently yesterday he was having some  emotional distress and called his family  his father flew out here from northern  california yesterday afternoon  late yesterday afternoon the family  tried to get a hold of the father and he  did not answer his phone and they could  not reach the sun either  that prompted the mother and another son  to fly to las vegas to check on both of  them that is when tonight the mother and  the son came to the residence and that's  when they discovered  the body of  the victim laying inside the house so  again at this point it is still very  active investigation our suspect again  again is believed to be a 30 year old  black male who is the son of the  deceased and we are trying to locate him  at this point so anybody who does have  any information i please ask you to  reach out to crime stoppers your  information is completely anonymous and  there's also reward money available so  with that i'll take a couple questions  if you have them so why didn't police  enter the house first  before  the family  went inside so the original details that  were provided there were some details  that could not be corroborated which  ended up being false information that  was originally provided so the officers  attempted to validate that information  and were not able to validate it at that  point that's why officers did not enter  the residence when they first came on  the original call any indication how the  victim died right now there's  the original  belief is that it's going to be  potentially from gunshots however we  have not val verified that we're in the  process of obtaining a search warrant so  we can get inside the residence and the  coroner will make that determination but  there is some evidence that does show  that gun shots uh were fired inside the  house clarification on the timeline here  neighbors are saying that police first  responded to this neighborhood like 3 30  today and then  completely left the area and then around  five o'clock the family entered the home  and they found the male deceased and  they believe that that male had been  there for some time so the information  that was provided originally to the  officers when the family got here there  was some information that was  we have learned has not was not factual  so that information was provided to  officers officers attempted to look  inside the residence to validate some of  the information that they were provided  when they could not do that there was no  exigency that the patrol officers were  able to make at that time to enter the  house it is after the officers left when  the family  entered the house and actually  discovered the victim inside the house  do we know if the suspect drove off  walked off  people should be looking for we we're  trying to find that out right now  there's still like i said a lot of  moving parts the vehicle his vehicle is  still at the residence so we're still  trying to figure out how he left the  residence  is the family saying that he had a  history of mental distress mental  illness the family is stating that there  is a potential mental illness issue i  don't know if he's been diagnosed with  any mental illness but according to the  family he does have some mental problems  do you have this description on the  suspect  again right now until we can complete  the investigation and get in and  execute the search warrant i'll just  leave it with a black male in his early  30s do you believe the victim was killed  today or possibly yesterday do you have  any sort of timeline on that until we  can actually get inside the house and  the coroner can examine the body that's  going to be our next step so we don't  know from that flight from northern  california in uh into vegas do you have  a timeline on like when he actually  arrived in the city so we know he  arrived yesterday so then again  listening to the family after i believe  it was 3 p.m yesterday is when they last  heard from him so we don't have a  specific timeline after that  right thank you guys i appreciate it

